│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ circular_skip_hea_ansatz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a linear chain of CZ gates and rotations (RY, RZ) which may limit │
│                          │ the expressivity and information flow across the 8-qubit register, especially given that  │
│                          │ the feature map uses IsingZZ couplings on varied qubit pairs.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose a more expressive Hardware-Efficient Ansatz (HEA) inspired structure:           │
│                          │ 1.  **Increased Connectivity**: Replacing the linear CZ chain with two layers of CNOT     │
│                          │ gates: a circular chain (neighboring qubits) and a skip-1 chain (0-2, 1-3, etc.). This    │
│                          │ ensures that information from any qubit can reach any other qubit much faster, improving  │
│                          │ the model's ability to capture complex feature correlations.                              │
│                          │ 2.  **Strategic Rotation Layers**: Using two RY layers and one RZ layer (24 parameters    │
│                          │ total per block). Since the feature map is Z-basis heavy, having multiple RY layers       │
│                          │ allows the circuit to effectively rotate the state into more expressive regions of the    │
│                          │ Hilbert space.                                                                            │
│                          │ 3.  **Parameter Parity**: The parameter count per block remains 24, identical to the      │
│                          │ seed. This ensures that any performance gain is due to the architectural improvement      │
│                          │ rather than just increasing the parameter budget.                                         │
