│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the fully independent per-qubit RY/RZ + line-CZ block with a more      │
│                          │ compact, higher-bias ansatz that is better suited to the fixed data-uploading pipeline.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main ideas:                                                                               │
│                          │ - Keep a strong initial local mixing layer with independent RY on all 8 qubits.           │
│                          │ - Replace the shallow nearest-neighbor entangler with a butterfly-style CZ pattern that   │
│                          │ mixes both long-range and local correlations.                                             │
│                          │ - Use parameter sharing on mirrored qubit pairs for the phase-correction and final        │
│                          │ readout-adaptation layers. This reduces the number of trainable circuit parameters per    │
│                          │ block while preserving symmetry and improving generalization.                             │
│                          │ - End the block with RY rather than RZ so the last operation is directly visible to the   │
│                          │ Z-basis readout, which usually improves trainability and validation/test accuracy.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall this should lower overfitting, improve parameter efficiency, and keep the circuit │
│                          │ expressive enough for the 6 repeated blocks induced by the fixed l=3, p=2 layout.         │
