│ patch_description        │ This restructuring introduces object-oriented architecture with clear separation of       │
│                          │ concerns:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **CircuitManager class**: Encapsulates gate specification, validation, and parameter   │
│                          │ mapping, eliminating the monolithic validation and parameter tracking logic. Handles      │
│                          │ parameter registration and efficient lookups.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **QuantumClassifier class**: Wraps the quantum circuit and classical readout,          │
│                          │ providing a clean interface for prediction and loss computation. Centralizes parameter    │
│                          │ initialization strategy and improves numerical stability.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **ImprovedAnsatz design**: Adopts controlled rotation gates (CRX/CRY) with shared      │
│                          │ parameters across qubits to reduce parameter count while maintaining expressiveness. Uses │
│                          │ a ring topology with controlled two-qubit interactions instead of a linear chain,         │
│                          │ improving connectivity and entanglement.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Optimized training loop**: Extracted into a separate TrainingContext class with      │
│                          │ better convergence tracking and parameter checkpointing.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Efficiency gains**:                                                                  │
│                          │    - Reduced circuit depth through parameter sharing and efficient gate patterns          │
│                          │    - Better parameter initialization with proper scaling                                  │
│                          │    - Cleaner parameter-to-gate mapping reduces overhead                                   │
│                          │    - Improved numerical stability in loss computation                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structural changes maintain backward compatibility with the fixed training interface  │
│                          │ while improving modularity, maintainability, and performance through better parameter     │
│                          │ efficiency and circuit design.                                                            │
