│ patch_name               │ butterfly_mixer_rx_readout                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets two weaknesses in the seed block.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ First, the original final RZ layer is effectively measurement-invariant for the Z         │
│                          │ readout, so it adds parameters without improving the classifier signal. I replace that    │
│                          │ terminal RZ layer with an RX layer, which directly changes the measured Z expectations    │
│                          │ and gives the last stage real predictive power.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Second, the original entanglement is only a nearest-neighbor chain. Since the fixed       │
│                          │ feature map already uses arbitrary qubit pairs, the ansatz should also be able to mix     │
│                          │ distant qubits efficiently. I replace the line of CZ gates with a butterfly-style         │
│                          │ all-to-all mixing pattern over long, medium, and short-range pairs. This should better    │
│                          │ capture cross-feature correlations, improve validation/test accuracy, and reduce          │
│                          │ overfitting without increasing parameter count.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The parameter budget stays the same: 24 trainable parameters per block, but the block is  │
│                          │ more expressive where it matters.                                                         │
