│ patch_name               │ add_cry_layer_to_current                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves the best combined score (0.07) with excellent parameter      │
│                          │ efficiency (only 74 params total, yielding 12 params per block). However, test accuracy   │
│                          │ is slightly lower (0.86) compared to the seed (0.88).                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current ansatz uses parameter sharing for single-qubit gates and a ring of CRX        │
│                          │ entangling gates. To improve test accuracy while maintaining parameter efficiency, I will │
│                          │ add a parametrized CRY layer in addition to the existing CRX ring. This provides          │
│                          │ additional expressivity for entanglement without dramatically increasing parameter count. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new structure will be:                                                                │
│                          │ - RY layer with shared parameters (2 unique params: ry_a, ry_b)                           │
│                          │ - CRX ring connectivity (8 params: crx_0 through crx_7)                                   │
│                          │ - CRY ring connectivity (8 params: cry_0 through cry_7) - NEW                             │
│                          │ - RZ layer with shared parameters (2 unique params: rz_c, rz_d)                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Total unique parameters per block: 20 (up from 12)                                        │
│                          │ Total circuit parameters: 120 (up from 72)                                                │
│                          │ Total parameters including readout: 122 (up from 74)                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This modest increase should improve model expressivity and test accuracy while keeping    │
│                          │ parameter efficiency competitive.                                                         │
