│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the current fully local, over-parameterized block with a more          │
│                          │ structured low-parameter ansatz that is better matched to the mean-Z readout and the      │
│                          │ feature-map-induced ZZ phases.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Use mirror-symmetric shared single-qubit rotations to reduce redundant degrees of       │
│                          │ freedom and improve generalization.                                                       │
│                          │ - Insert a trainable long-range CRY entangling layer to adaptively mix feature-induced    │
│                          │ correlations.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Keep a fixed CZ ring as a cheap second entangling path to preserve expressivity without │
│                          │ increasing parameter count.                                                               │
│                          │ - Maintain a compact 12-parameter-per-block budget, which should help validation/test     │
│                          │ stability and convergence speed compared with the current 16-parameter block.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result keeps the architecture valid, stays within the supported gate set, and should  │
│                          │ improve the accuracy/gap tradeoff while lowering depth and parameter count.               │
