│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ untie_outer_ry                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz already performs well, but it still enforces a hard symmetry on the    │
│                          │ outer qubits by sharing the same `ry_out_0` parameter between wires 0 and 7. That         │
│                          │ symmetry may be too restrictive for this dataset, especially because the fixed feature    │
│                          │ map is asymmetric across qubit pairs.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit makes one small, controlled relaxation: it splits the outer `RY` sharing into   │
│                          │ two independent parameters, `ry_out_0a` and `ry_out_0b`, while keeping the rest of the    │
│                          │ compact layered structure unchanged. This preserves the efficient topology and low        │
│                          │ parameter count regime, but gives the model just enough extra expressive power to fit     │
│                          │ asymmetric decision boundaries and potentially improve validation/test accuracy without   │
│                          │ materially increasing overfitting risk.                                                   │
