│ patch_name               │ symmetric_mirrored_calibration_ansatz                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This redesigned ansatz utilizes a symmetric, hardware-efficient structure with parameter  │
│                          │ sharing across mirrored qubit pairs (0-7, 1-6, 2-5, 3-4) to improve generalization and    │
│                          │ reduce the train-test gap.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key structural features:                                                                  │
│                          │ 1.  **Mirrored Parameter Sharing**: RX, RY, and RZ layers share parameters between qubits │
│                          │ equidistant from the center of the 8-qubit chain. This enforces a symmetry that reflects  │
│                          │ common data patterns and improves parameter efficiency.                                   │
│                          │ 2.  **Calibration RZ Layer**: Following the system recommendation, a trainable RZ layer   │
│                          │ is placed at the end of the block. In a re-uploading scheme, this acts as a corrective    │
│                          │ phase adjustment immediately preceding the next feature injection.                        │
│                          │ 3.  **Hybrid Entanglement**: Combines a fixed CNOT ring for robust state mixing with a    │
│                          │ parametrized CRZ ring (also using mirrored sharing) to provide fine-tuned control over    │
│                          │ entanglement strength.                                                                    │
│                          │ 4.  **Diverse Rotation Bases**: Utilizes RX, RY, and RZ rotations within every block to   │
│                          │ ensure the ansatz can explore the full Bloch sphere effectively, translating the phase    │
│                          │ information from the IsingZZ feature map into measurable Z-expectations.                  │
