│ patch_name               │ mirror_butterfly_crz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ I redesigned the ansatz as a symmetric, low-parameter “shell + butterfly +                │
│                          │ phase-correction” block. The block uses mirrored RY and RX layers to keep the circuit     │
│                          │ expressive but regularized, a fixed CZ butterfly to spread correlations across the        │
│                          │ register, and two shared CRZ links to add trainable phase selectivity on the strongest    │
│                          │ entangling paths. This keeps the circuit efficient, reduces overfitting pressure, and     │
│                          │ makes the final block directly visible to the Z readout because it ends with RX instead   │
│                          │ of a trailing RZ layer.                                                                   │
