│ patch_description        │ The current program has 146 parameters (24 per block) which is too high and leads to      │
│                          │ worse performance than the second program (98 params, 16 per block, score 0.23) despite   │
│                          │ having more parameters. This indicates overfitting and poor parameter efficiency.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to reduce back to ~16 parameters per block by:                      │
│                          │ 1. Removing the redundant individual RZ-pre layer (8 params) that adds little value       │
│                          │ 2. Removing the individual RX-post layer (8 params) that duplicates functionality         │
│                          │ 3. Adopting the proven parameter-sharing structure from the second program:               │
│                          │    - Individual RY on each qubit for input flexibility (8 params)                         │
│                          │    - Fixed CZ gates for entanglement: diagonal pairs [0,4],[1,5],[2,6],[3,7] plus local   │
│                          │ adjacent pairs                                                                            │
│                          │    - RZ layer with 2-qubit parameter sharing by symmetry: 4 params shared across          │
│                          │ mirror-symmetric qubit pairs                                                              │
│                          │    - RY layer with 2-qubit parameter sharing: 4 params shared across mirror-symmetric     │
│                          │ qubit pairs                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces to 16 params/block (96 total circuit params) which matches the               │
│                          │ best-performing second program, reducing overfitting while maintaining expressive power   │
│                          │ through diverse fixed CZ connectivity and strategic parameter sharing.                    │
