│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_symmetric_crz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This hybrid crossover combines the best aspects of the high-performing programs (Program  │
│                          │ 1/3 with score 0.23) with structured parametrized entanglement to improve expressivity.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key design decisions:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. **Input layer**: Keep individual RY parameters per qubit (8 params) from Programs 1/3, │
│                          │ which provides better feature encoding than shared parameters.                            │
│                          │ 2. **Fixed entanglement**: Retain the diagonal (long-range) and local CZ pattern from     │
│                          │ Programs 1/3, which achieves better test accuracy than the ring topology in Program 2.    │
│                          │ 3. **Parametrized entanglement**: Add parametrized CRZ gates on diagonal pairs to enhance │
│                          │ expressivity with controlled two-qubit interactions, enabling better feature mixing       │
│                          │ during optimization.                                                                      │
│                          │ 4. **Output structure**: Maintain the mirror-symmetric shared parameters for RZ and RY    │
│                          │ layers (4 unique params each), which balance model capacity with generalization.          │
│                          │ 5. **Parameter efficiency**: Total of 20 params per block (8 input RY + 4 diagonal CRZ +  │
│                          │ 4 RZ + 4 output RY), resulting in 120 circuit params + 2 readout = 122 total params. This │
│                          │ is between the efficient Program 2 (98) and allows more expressivity.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added CRZ gates on diagonal pairs (0-4, 1-5, 2-6, 3-7) provide parametrized two-qubit │
│                          │ rotations that complement the fixed CZ gates, potentially improving the model's ability   │
│                          │ to learn complex feature correlations while maintaining the symmetry structure that       │
│                          │ worked well in prior programs.                                                            │
