│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ complement_entanglement_crz                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests alternating between two mirror-symmetric CZ mesh patterns to  │
│                          │ diversify entanglement pathways. While full alternation across blocks cannot be           │
│                          │ implemented within ANSATZ_SPEC alone, we can incorporate both patterns within each block  │
│                          │ by adding parametrized CRZ gates on the complementary long-range diagonal [0,5], [1,4],   │
│                          │ [2,7], [3,6].                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Enriches the entanglement topology by combining the primary long-range diagonal [0,4], │
│                          │ [1,5], [2,6], [3,7] with its complementary pattern                                        │
│                          │ 2. Uses shared CRZ parameters (crz_comp_outer and crz_comp_inner) to maintain parameter   │
│                          │ efficiency                                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Introduces only 2 new trainable parameters per block (12 total across all blocks),     │
│                          │ scaling the total to ~110 parameters                                                      │
│                          │ 4. Improves expressivity for capturing broader qubit correlations without excessive       │
│                          │ growth in circuit depth                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The placement after local CZ gates and before the middle RZ layer allows the              │
│                          │ complementary entanglement to interact with the local structure before phase mixing,      │
│                          │ potentially improving both convergence speed and generalization by providing richer       │
│                          │ pathways for information flow during data re-uploading.                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0451                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
