╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mirror_pair_readout_rich_ansatz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses excessive parameter sharing in the ansatz (only 74 total params) │
│                          │ which reduces expressivity despite faster convergence. The prior programs achieved 0.87   │
│                          │ test accuracy with 98 parameters using more individual parameters in input/output layers  │
│                          │ plus mirror-symmetry sharing.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Richer Ansatz**: Restore individual RY input parameters (8 params) instead of just 2 │
│                          │ shared params; keep ring CRX connectivity but with 4 mirror-shared params instead of 8    │
│                          │ unique; add 4 mirror-shared RZ params and 4 mirror-shared output RY params. This yields   │
│                          │ ~20 params/block × 6 blocks = 120 circuit params.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Mirror-Pair Readout Calibration**: Replace global gain/bias (2 params) with          │
│                          │ per-mirror-pair calibration (8 params). After computing 8 Z-expectations, average them    │
│                          │ over pairs (0&7), (1&6), (2&5), (3&4) to get 4 values, then apply independent             │
│                          │ gain_i/bias_i to each pair before taking the final mean. This finer-grained calibration   │
│                          │ mirrors the ansatz symmetry and should improve convergence speed while maintaining        │
│                          │ per-block parameter efficiency.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Target: ~128 total parameters, better than current 74 (too sparse) but close to prior 98  │
│                          │ (which had good generalization), with tighter train-test gap via symmetric readout.       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0581                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
