│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mirrored_crxcz_block                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses only 8 trainable keys per block and relies on two CZ ladders plus │
│                          │ mirrored RY/RZ layers, which gives limited expressivity for the fixed ZZ feature map.     │
│                          │ This rewrite keeps the same training loop and measurement pipeline, but changes the block │
│                          │ to a more balanced 12-parameter design: mirrored RY pre-rotations, long-range CZ mixing,  │
│                          │ mixed-axis controlled rotations (CRX/CRY/CRZ), mirrored RZ phase refinement, and a final  │
│                          │ local CNOT mixer.                                                                         │
│                          │ The key idea is to preserve parameter sharing across mirrored qubits while adding a small │
│                          │ controlled-rotation core that can capture higher-order feature correlations faster and    │
│                          │ with less overfitting pressure than the previous purely CZ-based pattern.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0582                                                                                   │
