│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_local_crz_scaffold                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz utilizes a fixed entangling scaffold composed of four long-range CZ    │
│                          │ gates and four local CZ gates. To improve the circuit's ability to learn specific         │
│                          │ correlations between adjacent qubits while maintaining parameter efficiency, I am         │
│                          │ replacing the four local CZ gates ([0,1], [2,3], [4,5], [6,7]) with two pairs of          │
│                          │ mirror-shared CRZ rotations. Specifically, one parameter 'crz_loc_0' is shared between    │
│                          │ the outer local pairs (0,1) and (6,7), and another parameter 'crz_loc_1' is shared        │
│                          │ between the inner local pairs (2,3) and (4,5). This hybrid approach grants the model      │
│                          │ tunable Z-axis entanglement at the local level—complementing the global entanglement      │
│                          │ provided by the fixed long-range CZ gates—potentially improving the validation loss and   │
│                          │ overall classification accuracy.                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
