│ patch_description        │ This edit introduces a dual-stage entanglement strategy within each ansatz block. It      │
│                          │ replaces the simple repeated rotation layers with a more expressive configuration:        │
│                          │ 1.  **Mirrored RY Pre-rotations**: Compactly lifts features into the Hilbert space (4     │
│                          │ parameters).                                                                              │
│                          │ 2.  **Local CZ Scaffold**: Provides initial spatial mixing between adjacent qubits.       │
│                          │ 3.  **Mixed-Axis Core 1 (CRX-CRY-CRZ-CRY)**: Introduces non-commuting controlled          │
│                          │ rotations for high expressivity (4 parameters).                                           │
│                          │ 4.  **Mirrored RZ Post-rotations**: Refines the phase before the next entanglement stage  │
│                          │ (4 parameters).                                                                           │
│                          │ 5.  **Mixed-Axis Core 2 (CRZ-CRX-CRY-CRX)**: Cycles the rotation axes over the same qubit │
│                          │ pairs to capture complex correlations (4 parameters).                                     │
│                          │ 6.  **Global CZ Scaffold**: Ensures long-range entanglement between the two 4-qubit       │
│                          │ halves of the register.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By using 16 unique parameters per block (98 total for the circuit), this design balances  │
│                          │ parameter efficiency with a significantly higher entanglement capacity, aiming to improve │
│                          │ test accuracy and convergence speed while maintaining a depth well below the limit.       │
