│ patch_name               │ mirror_shared_crz_mix                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This edit strengthens the ansatz by making the long-range entangling scaffold trainable   │
│                          │ instead of fixed: the four distant CZ links are replaced by two mirror-shared CRZ         │
│                          │ parameters, so the circuit can learn the entanglement strength while preserving the same  │
│                          │ symmetric structure. To keep the model parameter-efficient and reduce overfitting, one    │
│                          │ redundant mid-circuit controlled rotation is removed and its role is absorbed into the    │
│                          │ shared CRZ symmetry. The result keeps the block compact, maintains mirror bias that       │
│                          │ worked well in prior programs, and should improve validation/test accuracy with similar   │
│                          │ or better convergence behavior.                                                           │
