│ patch_description        │ The proposed ansatz evolves the high-performing mirror-symmetric structure of the seed    │
│                          │ programs by incorporating a diverse mixed-axis controlled-rotation core. Key parameters   │
│                          │ are the mirrord single-qubit rotations (RY for input lifting and RZ for output phase      │
│                          │ refinement) which utilize parameter sharing to keep the model efficient. The entanglement │
│                          │ layer is enhanced by combining fixed long-range CZ gates with parameterized mixed-axis    │
│                          │ couplings: shared long-range CRZ gates for global coordination and shared local CRX/CRY   │
│                          │ gates for neighborhood interactions. This configuration maintains the parameter           │
│                          │ efficiency of the original 74-parameter model (12 parameters per block) while increasing  │
│                          │ the expressivity of the entanglement layer to improve test accuracy and convergence       │
│                          │ speed.                                                                                    │
