│ patch_name               │ asymmetric_post_rz_split                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This edit introduces a controlled symmetry break in the final layer of the ansatz block.  │
│                          │ By releasing the parameter sharing for the RZ gates on qubits 2 and 5 (previously shared  │
│                          │ as 'rz_g2'), we provide the model with a slightly larger hypothesis space to calibrate    │
│                          │ the readout signals of the central qubits independently. The other three pairs (0/7, 1/6, │
│                          │ 3/4) remain mirror-shared to maintain parameter efficiency and regularization. This       │
│                          │ targeted increase in expressive power aims to reduce the generalization gap and improve   │
│                          │ validation accuracy by allowing more flexible phase refinement before the final           │
│                          │ Z-measurement averaging.                                                                  │
