                         Patch Metadata - Gen 41/50 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_cr_entanglement                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz achieves good test accuracy (0.87) but has relatively low parameter    │
│                          │ efficiency (0.01).                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of the prior programs shows that parameter sharing via mirror symmetry improved  │
│                          │ the combined score from 0.23 to 0.27 while reducing n_params from 98 to 74. The fixed     │
│                          │ circuit architecture (N_REPEATS=2, N_UPLOADS=3) and the constraint that we can only       │
│                          │ modify ANSATZ_SPEC means I cannot implement parameter sharing across repeats at the code  │
│                          │ level.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ However, I can enhance the ansatz expressivity by adding a second layer of parameterized  │
│                          │ controlled rotations on complementary qubit pairs. This increases the capacity of the     │
│                          │ ansatz to learn feature interactions without drastically increasing the parameter count   │
│                          │ per block.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy is to:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Keep the existing pre-rotation, entangling scaffold, and post-rotation layers          │
│                          │ 2. Insert an additional controlled-rotation layer between the first and second            │
│                          │ controlled-rotation layers, targeting orthogonal qubit pairs (0-2, 1-3, 4-6, 5-7)         │
│                          │ 3. Reuse some parameters where symmetry allows, adding only 2 new parameters (crz_b,      │
│                          │ crx_c)                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 12 to 14, and total params from 74 to 14*3*2+2 =   │
│                          │ 86.                                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The intuition: deeper controlled-rotation layers with different pair connectivity enhance │
│                          │ entanglement patterns and feature extraction across multiple scales, potentially          │
│                          │ improving test accuracy and reducing the generalization gap without excessive             │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0436                                                                                   │
