│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parameter_sharing_simplification                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current architecture (110 parameters) underperforms compared to the prior programs    │
│                          │ (74 parameters, combined_score 0.27 vs 0.13). The issue is over-parameterization: the     │
│                          │ current ANSATZ_SPEC uses 18 unique parameters per block, compared to 12 in the prior      │
│                          │ architecture.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ While the formal recommendation to tie parameters across repeats within                   │
│                          │ `apply_ansatz_block` would require modifying code outside EVOLVE-BLOCK markers (which is  │
│                          │ prohibited), we can instead simplify the ANSATZ_SPEC to use more aggressive parameter     │
│                          │ sharing, reducing to approximately 10 unique parameters per block.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Return to the mirror-symmetric parameter sharing pattern from prior programs (which    │
│                          │ achieved 0.27 combined_score)                                                             │
│                          │ 2. Replace the 8-gate CRZ ring with a fixed-gate CZ scaffold (reducing controlled         │
│                          │ rotations from 8 to 4)                                                                    │
│                          │ 3. Consolidate RY and RZ layers to use 2 shared parameters each instead of 4              │
│                          │ 4. This reduces N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 18 to 10, cutting total params from 110 to ~62    │
│                          │ (plus 2 readout = 64)                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This aligns with the parameter efficiency insight: the prior 74-param architecture was    │
│                          │ already over-parameterized, so reducing further should help unless it sacrifices          │
│                          │ expressivity. By combining the CZ scaffold (proven architecture) with mirror symmetry     │
│                          │ (proven parameter sharing), we recover efficiency while maintaining expressivity.         │
