                         Patch Metadata - Gen 45/50 - Novelty: 2/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_mirror_entangling_ansatz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best architectural insights from both programs:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the seed program (score 0.27)**: Takes the superior ANSATZ_SPEC featuring:      │
│                          │    - Mirror-symmetric RY pre-rotations on qubit pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7)                │
│                          │    - Long-range + local CZ entangling scaffold (fixed gates)                              │
│                          │    - Mixed-axis controlled rotations (CRX, CRY, CRZ) for expressiveness                   │
│                          │    - Mirrored RZ post-rotations for readout calibration                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Rationale**: The seed achieves validation_accuracy of 0.91 vs current's 0.88 (same   │
│                          │ test accuracy 0.87-0.88 but much better validation). The structured mirror symmetry and   │
│                          │ mixed-axis CR gates provide better feature expressiveness despite having the same         │
│                          │ parameter count.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Expected improvements**:                                                             │
│                          │    - Higher validation accuracy (0.91 vs 0.88)                                            │
│                          │    - Better generalization with fixed entangling scaffold                                 │
│                          │    - Same parameter efficiency (74 params) but better quality                             │
│                          │    - Reduced circuit depth while maintaining expressiveness                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix is straightforward: replace the current ring-based CRZ topology with the proven   │
│                          │ mirror-symmetric + long-range/local CZ + mixed-axis CR structure from the higher-scoring  │
